# Copy to .env. Never commit .env.
# .env is gitignored. Check that it still is before you add a key.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ path. Cheap, keyless, high volume tolerated badly but fine for reads.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for: preflight, on-chain checks, operator expiry polling, ad-hoc cast
# calls. Anything that makes a handful of requests and does not fork.
#
# evm.stupidtech.net races 5 random public providers per request and returns
# the first answer. Verified 2026-10-22: Sepolia ETHRegistrar.GRACE_PERIOD
# returned 2,419,200, matching a direct read. The winning upstream comes back
# in the x-rpc-provider header.
#
# LIMIT: 60 requests per 10 seconds per IP. Do not point a fork at this.
MAINNET_READ_RPC_URL=https://<keyless-public-rpc>
SEPOLIA_READ_RPC_URL=https://<keyless-public-rpc>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORK path. Needs a dedicated provider key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for: anvil --fork-url, and the Foundry test matrix.
#
# A fork fetches state lazily on every slot it touches, so the nine tests will
# exceed any shared rate limit in seconds. A racer is also wrong here: it
# answers from a different provider each call, so archive depth varies.
# One consistent upstream, one key.
#
# Get one from Alchemy or Infura, or self-host evm.stupidtech.net, which
# removes both problems.
# The key lives IN the URL, so these two are SECRETS, unlike the READ pair
# above. There is no separate key variable: that is the shape Alchemy,
# Infura and Foundry all use. Never copy one into app/.env, where Vite
# would inline it into the shipped bundle.
MAINNET_RPC_URL=https://<provider>/<YOUR-API-KEY>
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://<provider>/<YOUR-API-KEY>

# The local fork, once anvil is running against SEPOLIA_RPC_URL.
#
# Confirm the port before trusting this default: anvil picks the next free
# port if 8545 is already held by something else on your machine, and this
# project hit exactly that once (progress/contracts.md S2). Check with
# `lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN | grep anvil` and match it here, not the other
# way around.
LOCAL_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545

# Comma-separated labels (not full names) the operator watches, e.g.
# "estmcmxci" for estmcmxci.eth. No default: operator/node.ts and
# operator/worker.ts both fail loudly if this is unset or empty rather than
# guessing a name.
WATCHED_LABELS=autorenewdemo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keys. Run `cast wallet new` THREE times.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three distinct addresses:
#   1. DEPLOYER  deploys the stack, owns the demo name, holds the payment token
#   2. SESSION   the operator's key, the one the policy constrains
#   3. FALLBACK  where payments route when renewal fails for want of funds
#
# See AGENTS.md hard rules 2 and 3.
# Never 0x1C2F...fF21, which is compromised. Never the estmcmxci.eth owner.
DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=0x<64-hex-private-key-generate-a-fresh-one>
SESSION_PRIVATE_KEY=0x<64-hex-private-key-generate-a-fresh-one>

# The address written to the name's address record when renewal fails for want
# of funds.
#
# Keep this distinct from the session key. The session key belongs to the
# automation; routing payments there contradicts what the demo shows, which is
# that funds reach an address the OWNER controls when the funding wallet dies.
#
# No private key is needed. Nothing signs as the fallback, so the third
# wallet's key can be discarded. Any address you already control works.
FALLBACK_ADDRESS=0x<40-hex-ADDRESS-not-a-key>

# Optional, for verifying the Sepolia deployment.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=<etherscan-api-key>
